 "_doc": "What the doer's computer lane (assistant/doer/computer.py) may run on this PC. Enforced by computer_policy.py as a PreToolUse hook on every Bash / Write / Edit call of the headless turn, so the tier is decided by code, not by the model. Tier A: read-only -> run. Tier B: a write inside write_roots, a copy, a folder, a tool script that passes the scan -> run and report. Tier C: a delete or move outside write_roots, a write outside write_roots, installing software, killing a process, anything that sends over the network, git commit/push -> the hook refuses and the model must post a checkpoint card; the owner's tap re-runs the exact command (sha-bound) once. NEVER: refused outright, no card can unlock it. Paths are matched after ~ and relative paths are resolved; all patterns are case-insensitive regexes over the whole command text.",
